random_password Reveals Secret Content

### Terraform Version

```
Terraform v0.14.7
+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/null v3.1.0
+ provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/random v3.1.0
```

### Affected Resource(s)
- random_password

### Terraform Configuration Files

If you create a new dir, add the below content, and run terraform apply more than once, the terraform plan will reveal the result of random_password.

```hcl
terraform {
  required_providers {
    random = {
      source  = "hashicorp/random"
      version = "3.1.0"
    }
  }
}

variable "config_secret" {
  sensitive = true
  default   = "password123"
}

resource "random_password" "tell_noone" {
  length           = 16
  special          = true
  override_special = "_%@"
}

resource "null_resource" "reveal_to_me_your_secrets" {
  triggers = {
    revealed_secret = random_password.tell_noone.result
    hidden_secret   = var.config_secret
    always_trigger  = timestamp()

  }
}

```

### Expected Behavior

The password should not be revealed.

### Actual Behavior

The password appears in the plan:

```
Terraform will perform the following actions:

  # null_resource.reveal_to_me_your_secrets must be replaced
-/+ resource "null_resource" "reveal_to_me_your_secrets" {
      ~ id       = "4002335353332162042" -> (known after apply)
      ~ triggers = {
          - "always_trigger"  = "2021-03-05T15:38:12Z"
          - "hidden_secret"   = (sensitive)
          - "revealed_secret" = "@Nu7Ed7K7tP93STS"
        } -> (known after apply) # forces replacement
    }

Plan: 1 to add, 0 to change, 1 to destroy.
```

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Run `terraform init && terraform apply --auto-approve`
2. Run `terraform plan` -> The plan will reveal the output of the secret

This applies for other resources (e.g. `helm_release`) as well but this test case is the most straightforward.

### References
https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform/issues/27995

random_integer should accept min == max

### Affected Resource(s)
- random_integer

### Terraform Configuration Files
```hcl
data "alicloud_zones" "available" {
  available_instance_type = var.instance_type
  enable_details          = true
}

resource "random_integer" "zone_index" {
  min = 0
  max = length(data.alicloud_zones.available.zones) - 1
  keepers = {
    instance_type = var.instance_type
  }
}

locals {
  zone = data.alicloud_zones.available.zones[random_integer.zone_index.result]
}
```

### Expected Behavior
Choose a random AZ that has the specified instance type available.

### Actual Behavior
When there is only one AZ that provides the specified instance type, `random_integer` refuses to generate an index of zero for me.

### References
https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-random/blob/73e21bef24618f9a90d2e9eb63c99c5da187dbf9/internal/provider/resource_integer.go#L78-L80
